                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "A simple, old zombie game with strong focus on gameplay. It has 2 modes, one is objective based: inflitrate a facility, complete the quests and escape. Another mode is just to kill x amount of zombies before they run out of lives. The game has a very limited ammo and carrying ability. You cannot hoard all guns and ammo. The weapons are also very distinctive and pleasant to use. Are you good with headshots? Take the revolver. Want to have a better chances to survive in small corridors with zombies jumping from around the corner? Take a shotty. Ammo is also spread around the map. Sometime you take a gun but never ammo for it. Other times, you find 2 packs of rifle ammo but get killed before you find the rifle. The maps themselves are purely genius. Remember levolution in BF3 BF4? Children's play compared to zps. Imagine going down to an underwater facility, and then begin to escape when water begins to rise. As you nervously gather at the elevators, all you hope is that one guy behind pressed the button in control room. But it seems he was killed by the zombies camping there. Water begins to rise, human team stocked on ammo bravely keeps them at bay. And then one buy one players suffocate as the water reached the ceiling. All maps are unique, offering insanely complex and fun to play. After playing this game, I find most modern games' maps bland and boring. Idk if there are any alive servers, but at the top of its popularity, we had a base of ~100 players who knew each other well. The games like this make me realize that I would never switch to PS or Xbox",
